#!/usr/bin/env node
// profile-set — writes the Pipeline of one project, the field workflow.pipeline of its profile.json, or
// with --field other fields of it (workflow.agents and agents — the agents of a ticket and the model and
// effort of each Harness agent role, profiles/README.md —, the commands, the ticket paths, the languages
// and the rest), and nothing else. bin/profile stays the reader that writes nothing; an editor, worfy's
// preset of a plan, its "Edit profile" form or any other caller writes them through this script.
//
//   profile-set [-C <dir>] --read                          prints JSON { name, path, pipeline, resolved, fingerprint }:
//                                                          the field as written (null without it), the
//                                                          Pipeline it resolves to, and its fingerprint
//   profile-set [-C <dir>] --expect <fingerprint> --set <json | ->
//                                                          writes the Pipeline (JSON; `-` — read it from stdin)
//   profile-set [-C <dir>] --expect <fingerprint> --reset  removes the field: the default Pipeline from then on
//   profile-set [-C <dir>] --expect <fingerprint> --move <full|silent> [--folder <absolute path>]
//                                                          moves the project's workflow files to the other mode and
//                                                          only then writes mode and workflow.folder (below)
//
//   With one or more `--field <name>` the same three act on those fields instead, and a fourth only checks:
//   --read prints { name, path, fields: { <name>: value | null }, fingerprint }; --set takes a JSON object
//   with exactly the named fields as keys; --reset removes them all; --check <json | -> takes what --set
//   takes, checks it as --set would and writes nothing: exit 0 with { ok: true }, exit 1 with the problems.
//   The fingerprint is of the named fields together (never null), so --expect takes the one that --read
//   printed.
//   A name is a field of the profile, dotted below the top ("tickets.path", "docs.context.path"); one
//   name inside another ("docs" and "docs.adr_dir") is refused. name, mode, schema, workflow.folder,
//   workflow.pipeline and an object holding one of them (workflow) are read but never written here: the
//   name holds the profile's folder, the mode and the Workflow folder move with the workflow files, the
//   Pipeline has the calls above. A field the schema closes (agents.orchestrator) is a usage error.
//   A value is checked by the draft schema's rules for that field (profiles/draft.schema.json, through
//   lib/draft-schema.cjs, the checker bin/project-connect uses); a field the schema has no rules for takes
//   any JSON value. The profile the change leaves is then checked by the rules bin/profile reads the gate,
//   CI and cross-machine fields by (lib/profile-rules.cjs): workflow.ci "batch" without
//   workflow.ci_batch_run, a relative workflow.e2e_lock or a cross_machine_gate without its fields is not
//   written (--set, --check), and neither is a --reset that leaves one. null leaves an absent field absent; on a field present in the file it removes the
//   field, unless the schema requires it in its object: then null is written, and checked like a value.
//   The objects on the way to a field are made when absent or null; one of another type (an old string
//   form) is a problem, exit 1. A refused value prints { ok: false, errors: [{ path, message }] } on
//   stdout and each problem on a line of stderr.
//
// The project is the one `bin/profile -C <dir>` finds (the current directory without -C); this script
// asks bin/profile for the profile's directory, so both name the same file.
//
// A write is checked with the rules bin/profile reads the field by (lib/pipeline.cjs): a Pipeline that
// breaks one is not written. It goes ahead only while the file still has the Pipeline the caller read:
// --expect takes the fingerprint --read printed (`null` — the field was absent). Then the change is
// committed in the git repository of the Harness home, as bin/project-connect commits a new profile.
// Writers of one profile take turns: a lock folder next to profile.json is held from reading the file
// to the end of the commit. A writer killed from outside (SIGKILL, taskkill /F, a caller's timeout)
// leaves it behind; the next writer takes it over once it is 60 s old.
// A commit that cannot be made — no repository there, git missing, the commit refused — does not undo
// the write: the commit is the history, not a condition. It is reported as a warning.
//
// --move is the one write of mode and workflow.folder: they say where the workflow files are, so they change
// only together with the files (lib/workflow-move.cjs holds the plan, the checks and the rollback). The
// fingerprint is of those two fields, as `--field mode --field workflow.folder --read` prints it. Before
// anything is written it refuses (exit 1, the reasons as { ok: false, errors }): the project already in that
// mode, Full mode for a project of several repositories, uncommitted changes or no branch in the
// repository or in the Workflow folder, a file already at its new place, an open PR of a ticket's branch (or
// gh unable to tell; $PROFILE_SET_GH names the gh to start, for the tests). Then the tracked workflow files
// are copied to the other side and committed there, removed with `git rm` on this side and committed, and the
// profile gets mode and workflow.folder (Silent mode: --folder, by default <profile folder>/workflow, made with
// `git init` when absent; Full mode: null). A failure on the way — the profile not written included — puts
// both sides back as they were, and the profile stays as it was. The output on 0 adds
// moved: { mode, folder, paths, files }. PROFILE_SET_MOVE_FAIL_AT (tests only): copy | to-commit |
// from-commit | profile — fail as that step starts.
//
// Exit codes: 0 — written (or nothing to change, or --read, or --check found nothing); 1 — the Pipeline or
// a field breaks a rule or is not JSON, the profile cannot be read or written: nothing written, the reason
// in stderr; 2 — usage
// error; 3 — the directory is in no registered project, or the project has no profile (bin/profile's
// code); 5 — the Pipeline in the file is not the one the caller read: nothing written; 6 — another
// profile-set held the profile's lock for the whole wait (10 s): nothing written, try again.
// Output on 0 after a write (stdout, JSON): { written, fingerprint, warning } — `written` false when
// the file already said that; `warning` null, or why the change was not committed (also a line
// "profile-set: warning: …" in stderr). On 5: { conflict: true, fingerprint } with the fingerprint now.
"use strict"

const fs = require("node:fs")
const path = require("node:path")
const { spawnSync } = require("node:child_process")
const { randomBytes } = require("node:crypto")
// The git to start and the Harness state folder, with the variables of an eval run (EVAL_GIT, EVAL_HARNESS_HOME).
const { git: GIT, harnessHome } = require("../hooks/eval-env.cjs")
const { pipelineProblem, pipelineField, resolvePipeline, pipelineFingerprint } = require("../lib/pipeline.cjs")
const { loadDraftSchema, validate, fieldSchema } = require("../lib/draft-schema.cjs")
// The rules bin/profile reads the gate, CI and cross-machine fields by: a value it would call a broken profile is not written.
const { profileProblems } = require("../lib/profile-rules.cjs")

const BIN = path.dirname(fs.realpathSync(__filename))
const USAGE = `usage: profile-set [-C <dir>] [--field <name>]... (--read | --expect <fingerprint|null> --set <json|-> | --expect <fingerprint|null> --reset | --field <name>... --check <json|->)
       profile-set [-C <dir>] --expect <fingerprint> --move <full|silent> [--folder <absolute path>]
exit: 0 written, read or checked, 1 invalid value or unreadable profile, 2 usage, 3 not a registered project / no profile, 5 the value changed since it was read, 6 another write held the lock (try again)`

const out = (s) => process.stdout.write(s.endsWith("\n") ? s : s + "\n")
const err = (s) => process.stderr.write(s.endsWith("\n") ? s : s + "\n")
const die = (code, msg) => {
    if (msg) err(`profile-set: ${msg}`)
    process.exit(code)
}
const usage = (msg) => {
    if (msg) err(`profile-set: ${msg}`)
    err(USAGE)
    process.exit(2)
}

// --- arguments -----------------------------------------------------------------
let mode = null
let given = null
let expect
let target = process.cwd()
// --move: the mode the workflow files move to, and the Workflow folder of Silent mode (null — the default one).
let moveTo = null
let moveFolder = null
// The fields of --field, in the order given; empty — workflow.pipeline, as without the option.
const fields = []
// Read, never written here: the profile's folder name, the mode and the Workflow folder (moved with the
// workflow files), the schema version, and the Pipeline, written by the calls without --field.
const READ_ONLY = ["name", "mode", "schema", "workflow.folder", "workflow.pipeline"]
const SEGMENT = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/
const NOT_KEYS = ["__proto__", "constructor", "prototype"]
const within = (inner, outer) => inner === outer || inner.startsWith(`${outer}.`)
const setMode = (m) => {
    if (mode) usage("only one of --read/--set/--reset/--check at a time")
    mode = m
}
const argv = process.argv.slice(2)
for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {
    const a = argv[i]
    switch (a) {
        case "--read":
        case "--reset":
            setMode(a.slice(2))
            break
        case "--move":
            setMode("move")
            moveTo = argv[++i]
            if (moveTo !== "full" && moveTo !== "silent") usage("--move takes full or silent")
            break
        case "--folder":
            moveFolder = argv[++i]
            if (!moveFolder) usage("--folder needs the absolute path of the Workflow folder")
            break
        case "--set":
        case "--check":
            setMode(a.slice(2))
            given = argv[++i]
            if (given === undefined) usage(`${a} needs the value as JSON, or - to read it from stdin`)
            break
        case "--expect":
            expect = argv[++i]
            if (expect === undefined || expect === "") usage("--expect needs the fingerprint --read printed, or null")
            break
        case "--field": {
            const f = argv[++i]
            if (f === undefined) usage("--field needs the name of a profile field")
            const keys = f.split(".")
            if (!keys.every((k) => SEGMENT.test(k) && !NOT_KEYS.includes(k))) usage(`--field takes a dotted name of a profile field (letters, digits, _ and -), not ${f}`)
            if (!fields.includes(f)) fields.push(f)
            break
        }
        case "-C":
            target = argv[++i]
            if (!target) usage("-C needs a directory")
            break
        case "-h":
        case "--help":
            out(USAGE)
            process.exit(0)
        default:
            usage(`unknown argument: ${a}`)
    }
}
if (!mode) usage("say what to do: --read, --set, --reset, --check or --move")
if (moveFolder !== null && mode !== "move") usage("--folder goes with --move")
if (mode === "move") {
    if (fields.length > 0) usage("--move writes mode and workflow.folder, and no --field")
    if (moveTo === "full" && moveFolder !== null) usage("--folder goes with --move silent: Full mode has no Workflow folder")
    if (moveFolder !== null && !path.isAbsolute(moveFolder)) usage(`--folder takes an absolute path, not ${moveFolder}`)
    fields.push("mode", "workflow.folder")
}
// What is written, in messages: the Pipeline, or the fields of --field.
const WHAT = fields.length === 0 ? "the Pipeline" : fields.join(", ")
if (mode === "check" && fields.length === 0) usage("--check goes with --field")
if ((mode === "read" || mode === "check") && expect !== undefined) usage("--expect goes with --set or --reset")
if (mode !== "read" && mode !== "check" && expect === undefined) usage(`--${mode} needs --expect: the fingerprint of ${WHAT} the change was made over (null when the Pipeline was absent)`)
for (const f of fields) {
    const other = fields.find((g) => g !== f && within(f, g))
    if (other !== undefined) usage(`--field ${f} lies inside --field ${other}: name one of them`)
    if (mode === "read" || mode === "move") continue
    const fixed = READ_ONLY.find((r) => within(r, f))
    if (fixed !== undefined) usage(`--field ${f}: ${fixed} is read, never written by --field${fixed === "workflow.pipeline" ? " (write the Pipeline without --field)" : ""}`)
}
// The draft schema, for the rules of the fields; only a write or a check of fields reads it.
let schema = null
if (fields.length > 0 && mode !== "read" && mode !== "move") {
    try {
        schema = loadDraftSchema().properties.profile
    } catch (e) {
        die(1, `the draft schema cannot be read: ${e.message}`)
    }
    for (const f of fields) if (fieldSchema(schema, f).closed) usage(`--field ${f}: the draft schema allows no such field`)
}

// --- the profile: the one bin/profile finds ------------------------------------------
// The node running this script, not the first `node` on PATH.
const found = spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(BIN, "profile"), "-C", target, "--dir"], { encoding: "utf8", windowsHide: true })
if (found.error) die(1, `bin/profile could not be started: ${found.error.message}`)
if (found.status !== 0) {
    process.stderr.write(found.stderr || "")
    process.exit(found.status === 3 || found.status === 2 ? found.status : 1)
}
const dir = found.stdout.replace(/\r?\n+$/, "")
const pjPath = path.join(dir, "profile.json")

// The profile as the file has it now: its text, the parsed object and the fingerprint of its Pipeline.
function readProfile() {
    let text
    let profile
    try {
        text = fs.readFileSync(pjPath, "utf8")
        profile = JSON.parse(text)
    } catch (e) {
        die(1, `cannot read ${pjPath}: ${e.message}`)
    }
    if (profile === null || typeof profile !== "object" || Array.isArray(profile)) die(1, `${pjPath} is not a JSON object`)
    const current = pipelineField(profile.workflow)
    return { text, profile, current, fingerprint: fields.length === 0 ? pipelineFingerprint(current) : fieldsFingerprint(fieldValues(profile)) }
}

// --- the fields of --field ------------------------------------------------------------------
const isObject = (v) => v !== null && typeof v === "object" && !Array.isArray(v)
/** The object that holds field `f` in `profile` and its last key; holder undefined when an object on the way is absent or not an object. */
function holderOf(profile, f) {
    const keys = f.split(".")
    const last = keys.pop()
    let at = profile
    for (const k of keys) at = isObject(at) && Object.hasOwn(at, k) ? at[k] : undefined
    return { holder: isObject(at) ? at : undefined, last }
}
/** The value of a field of --field as the file has it; null when absent. */
function fieldValue(profile, f) {
    const { holder, last } = holderOf(profile, f)
    return holder !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(holder, last) ? holder[last] : null
}
/** True when the file has the field (null included). */
function fieldPresent(profile, f) {
    const { holder, last } = holderOf(profile, f)
    return holder !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(holder, last)
}
/** The named fields as the file has them, in the order of --field. */
const fieldValues = (profile) => Object.fromEntries(fields.map((f) => [f, fieldValue(profile, f)]))
// The fingerprint of the named fields together: the canonical JSON of an object (pipelineFingerprint takes
// any value), so the order of --field does not change it, and it is never null.
const fieldsFingerprint = (values) => pipelineFingerprint(values)
/** What a value does to field `f` of `profile`: "absent" (null on an absent field), "remove", or "write". */
function effectOf(profile, f, v) {
    if (v !== null) return "write"
    if (!fieldPresent(profile, f)) return "absent"
    return fieldSchema(schema, f).required ? "write" : "remove"
}
/** The problems of the value of the fields, without the file: an object with exactly the named fields, each by the schema. */
function shapeProblems(value) {
    if (!isObject(value)) return [{ path: "", message: `the value is not a JSON object of ${WHAT}` }]
    const errors = []
    for (const k of Object.keys(value)) if (!fields.includes(k)) errors.push({ path: k, message: `not a field of this write (${WHAT})` })
    for (const f of fields) {
        if (!Object.hasOwn(value, f)) errors.push({ path: f, message: "missing; null removes the field" })
        else if (value[f] !== null) {
            const rules = fieldSchema(schema, f).schema
            if (rules !== null) errors.push(...validate(rules, value[f], f).map(({ path: p, message }) => ({ path: p, message })))
        }
    }
    return errors
}
/** The problems the file adds: null written where the schema requires the field, an object on the way of another type. */
function fileProblems(profile, value) {
    const errors = []
    for (const f of fields) {
        const v = value[f]
        const effect = effectOf(profile, f, v)
        if (effect === "absent") continue
        if (v === null && effect === "write") {
            const rules = fieldSchema(schema, f).schema
            if (rules !== null) errors.push(...validate(rules, null, f).map(({ path: p, message }) => ({ path: p, message })))
        }
        if (effect !== "write") continue
        const keys = f.split(".")
        let at = profile
        for (let i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) {
            const next = Object.hasOwn(at, keys[i]) ? at[keys[i]] : undefined
            if (next === undefined || next === null) break
            if (!isObject(next)) {
                errors.push({ path: keys.slice(0, i + 1).join("."), message: `is ${Array.isArray(next) ? "a list" : `a ${typeof next}`} in the profile, not an object: change it by hand first` })
                break
            }
            at = next
        }
    }
    return errors
}
/** Refuses the value: the problems on stdout as JSON and on stderr one per line, exit 1. */
function refuse(errors) {
    out(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, errors }))
    for (const e of errors) err(`profile-set: ${pjPath}: ${e.path ? `${e.path}: ` : ""}${e.message} — not written`)
    process.exit(1)
}
/** Sets field `f` of `profile` by its effect: the objects on the way made when absent or null. */
function apply(profile, f, v) {
    const effect = effectOf(profile, f, v)
    if (effect === "absent") return
    const keys = f.split(".")
    const last = keys.pop()
    let at = profile
    for (const k of keys) {
        if (!isObject(at[k])) {
            if (effect === "remove") return
            at[k] = {}
        }
        at = at[k]
    }
    if (effect === "remove") delete at[last]
    else at[last] = v
}
/** The problems bin/profile would refuse `profile` for after the fields of `value` are set; the profile is not changed. */
function resultProblems(profile, value) {
    const result = structuredClone(profile)
    for (const f of fields) apply(result, f, value[f])
    return profileProblems(result)
}
const nameOf = (profile) => (typeof profile.name === "string" && profile.name ? profile.name : path.basename(dir))

if (mode === "read" && fields.length > 0) {
    const { profile, fingerprint } = readProfile()
    out(JSON.stringify({ name: nameOf(profile), path: pjPath, fields: fieldValues(profile), fingerprint }))
    process.exit(0)
}
if (mode === "read") {
    const { profile, current, fingerprint } = readProfile()
    const resolved = resolvePipeline(profile.workflow)
    if (resolved.problem !== undefined) die(1, `${pjPath}: workflow.pipeline${resolved.problem} — broken profile`)
    out(JSON.stringify({ name: nameOf(profile), path: pjPath, pipeline: current ?? null, resolved: resolved.pipeline, fingerprint }))
    process.exit(0)
}

// --- the new value, read and checked before the profile is ---------------------------
// stdin first: a caller slow to send the Pipeline must not hold a fingerprint taken before another write.
let value = null
if (mode === "set" || mode === "check") {
    let text = given
    if (given === "-") {
        try {
            text = fs.readFileSync(0, "utf8")
        } catch (e) {
            die(1, `cannot read ${WHAT} from stdin: ${e.message}`)
        }
    }
    try {
        value = JSON.parse(text)
    } catch (e) {
        die(1, `${WHAT} is not JSON: ${e.message} — not written`)
    }
    if (fields.length > 0) {
        const problems = shapeProblems(value)
        if (problems.length > 0) refuse(problems)
    } else {
        const problem = pipelineProblem(value)
        if (problem !== null) die(1, `${pjPath}: workflow.pipeline${problem} — not written`)
    }
}
// --check: the value against the file as it is now, without the lock; nothing is written.
if (mode === "check") {
    const { profile } = readProfile()
    const problems = fileProblems(profile, value)
    if (problems.length > 0) refuse(problems)
    const broken = resultProblems(profile, value)
    if (broken.length > 0) refuse(broken)
    out(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }))
    process.exit(0)
}

// --- the lock: one writer of a profile at a time ---------------------------------------
// A folder next to profile.json, made with mkdir (atomic on every file system the Harness runs on), with
// an `owner` file inside holding this writer's token (pid and random). It is held from reading the
// profile to the end of the commit, so the compare, the write and the commit of two writers never
// interleave. It is released on exit, and only by the writer whose token it holds.
// A lock whose owner file (or folder, before the file is there) is older than LOCK_STALE_MS is one a
// killed writer left. A waiter takes it over without ever moving a live lock: it claims the stale folder
// with a file made with O_EXCL inside it, checks that the folder is still the lock (same inode, same
// token), and only then renames it to a name of its own and deletes it. Once a stale folder leaves the
// lock's name it never comes back, so a folder that is the lock after the claim was the lock when the
// claim was made, and the claim is in it; of the waiters that judged it stale, the one claim that
// succeeded goes on alone. The lock folder is missing only once the stale one is gone, so a writer that
// makes it in between is a plain new owner. Two waiters cannot both clear one stale lock, and neither
// moves or deletes the lock a new owner has just made.
// The limit: the folder is told by its inode and token. A stale lock without an owner file (its writer
// was killed between mkdir and writing the token) is told by the inode alone, and a file system that
// hands that inode to a new lock folder within the takeover could let it be taken for the stale one.
// And a waiter that sleeps longer than LOCK_STALE_MS between its check and its rename is taken for dead,
// the same assumption the whole lock rests on.
// A live lock is waited for up to LOCK_WAIT_MS, then the write gives up with exit 6.
const LOCK = path.join(dir, ".profile-set.lock")
const OWNER = path.join(LOCK, "owner")
const LOCK_STALE_MS = 60_000
// shortcut: a fixed wait; PROFILE_SET_LOCK_WAIT_MS exists for the tests only, redo when a caller needs its own wait.
const LOCK_WAIT_MS = Number(process.env.PROFILE_SET_LOCK_WAIT_MS) || 10_000
// For the tests only: a folder that orders two writers taking over one stale lock by events, not by time.
// On judging the lock stale this writer puts its token in `judged`, waits for a `go` file there (up to
// STALE_SYNC_WAIT_MS, then goes on), takes over and then creates `tried`.
const STALE_SYNC = process.env.PROFILE_SET_STALE_SYNC || ""
const STALE_SYNC_WAIT_MS = 30_000
const TOKEN = `${process.pid}-${randomBytes(8).toString("hex")}`
const pause = (ms) => Atomics.wait(new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4)), 0, 0, ms)
const inoOf = (folder) => {
    try {
        return fs.statSync(folder, { bigint: true }).ino
    } catch {
        return null
    }
}
const ownerOf = (folder, file = "owner") => {
    try {
        return fs.readFileSync(path.join(folder, file), "utf8")
    } catch {
        return null
    }
}
let locked = false
// The script is synchronous to its end, so a signal handler would never run: after Ctrl+C the default
// action ends it, and the lock is released by the next writer's stale check, as after a kill.
process.on("exit", () => {
    if (!locked || ownerOf(LOCK) !== TOKEN) return
    try {
        fs.rmSync(LOCK, { recursive: true, force: true })
    } catch {}
})
// For the tests only: with a `hold-<at>` file in the PROFILE_SET_STALE_SYNC folder, a takeover stops at the
// point `at`: it creates the file `<at>` and waits for `resume-<at>` (up to STALE_SYNC_WAIT_MS). The points:
// `checked` (the lock judged still stale, not claimed yet) and `moved` (the lock moved aside, not deleted) of
// a takeover, and `waiting`: the first time the writer finds a live lock, before its first pause.
function stopPoint(at) {
    if (STALE_SYNC === "" || !fs.existsSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, `hold-${at}`))) return
    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, at), "")
    const until = Date.now() + STALE_SYNC_WAIT_MS
    while (!fs.existsSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, `resume-${at}`)) && Date.now() < until) pause(20)
}
/** Takes over a lock judged stale; with PROFILE_SET_STALE_SYNC, at the test's signal. True when it did. */
function clearStale(token, ino) {
    if (STALE_SYNC === "") return takeOver(token, ino)
    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, "judged"), TOKEN)
    const until = Date.now() + STALE_SYNC_WAIT_MS
    while (!fs.existsSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, "go")) && Date.now() < until) pause(20)
    const done = takeOver(token, ino)
    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(STALE_SYNC, "tried"), "")
    return done
}
// A claim on a stale lock folder: a file made with O_EXCL inside it. A claim with this writer's token is its
// own, left by an earlier try. A claim older than LOCK_STALE_MS is one a waiter killed during its takeover
// left (or one asleep that long, taken for dead as a stale lock's owner is), and the next name is tried.
// Returns the claim's path, or null when another waiter holds the claim or the folder is gone.
function claimIn(folder) {
    for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
        const claim = path.join(folder, `takeover-${i}`)
        try {
            fs.writeFileSync(claim, TOKEN, { flag: "wx" })
            return claim
        } catch (e) {
            if (e.code !== "EEXIST") return null
        }
        if (ownerOf(folder, `takeover-${i}`) === TOKEN) return claim
        try {
            if (Date.now() - fs.statSync(claim).mtimeMs <= LOCK_STALE_MS) return null
        } catch {
            return null
        }
    }
}
/** Takes over the lock if it is still the stale one: folder `ino`, owner `token` (null: no owner file yet). True when it did. */
function takeOver(token, ino) {
    const stale = () => inoOf(LOCK) === ino && ownerOf(LOCK) === token
    if (!stale()) return false
    stopPoint("checked")
    // Making and removing the claim changes the folder's mtime, by which a stale lock without an owner file
    // is judged: a claim taken back puts the old times back, or the lock would look fresh for LOCK_STALE_MS.
    let times
    try {
        times = fs.statSync(LOCK)
    } catch {
        return false
    }
    const unclaim = (claim) => {
        try {
            fs.unlinkSync(claim)
            if (inoOf(LOCK) === ino) fs.utimesSync(LOCK, times.atime, times.mtime)
        } catch {}
    }
    const claim = claimIn(LOCK)
    if (claim === null) return false
    // Checked after the claim, not only before: the claim is in the stale folder only if that folder is the lock still.
    if (!stale()) {
        unclaim(claim)
        return false
    }
    const aside = `${LOCK}.stale-${TOKEN}`
    try {
        fs.renameSync(LOCK, aside)
    } catch {
        // Not moved (on Windows: a file in it is open): the claim goes, or every waiter would take it for another's.
        unclaim(claim)
        return false
    }
    stopPoint("moved")
    fs.rmSync(aside, { recursive: true, force: true })
    return true
}
const deadline = Date.now() + LOCK_WAIT_MS
let waited = false
while (!locked) {
    try {
        fs.mkdirSync(LOCK)
    } catch (e) {
        if (e.code !== "EEXIST") die(1, `cannot take the lock ${LOCK}: ${e.message} — not written`)
        const token = ownerOf(LOCK)
        const ino = inoOf(LOCK)
        let age = 0
        try {
            age = Date.now() - fs.statSync(token === null ? LOCK : OWNER).mtimeMs
        } catch {
            continue // gone in between: try again at once
        }
        if (ino === null) continue
        // Taken over: try at once. Not taken over (another waiter claimed it, or it changed): wait as for a live lock.
        if (age > LOCK_STALE_MS && clearStale(token, ino)) continue
        if (!waited) {
            waited = true
            // A test may release the lock at this point: try again at once, before the deadline is looked at.
            stopPoint("waiting")
            continue
        }
        if (Date.now() >= deadline) die(6, `another profile-set is writing ${pjPath} (lock ${LOCK}) — not written; try again`)
        pause(100)
        continue
    }
    try {
        fs.writeFileSync(OWNER, TOKEN)
    } catch (e) {
        try {
            fs.rmdirSync(LOCK)
        } catch {}
        die(1, `cannot take the lock ${LOCK}: ${e.message} — not written`)
    }
    locked = true
}

// --- the move of the workflow files (--move), under the lock ------------------------------
/**
 * Plans and runs the move over `profile` (read under the lock), then sets mode and workflow.folder in it;
 * refuses (exit 1) before any write when the plan has problems. Returns the report and the undo of the files.
 */
function moveFiles() {
    const { planMove, runMove, undoMove } = require("../lib/workflow-move.cjs")
    const shown = spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(BIN, "profile"), "-C", target, "--json"], { encoding: "utf8", windowsHide: true })
    let resolved = null
    try {
        resolved = shown.status === 0 ? JSON.parse(shown.stdout)._resolved : null
    } catch {}
    if (!isObject(resolved)) die(1, `bin/profile --json could not be read (exit ${shown.status}): ${(shown.stderr || "").trim().split("\n")[0]} — nothing moved`)
    const { problems, plan } = planMove({ profile, resolved, to: moveTo, folder: moveFolder, profileDir: dir, gh: process.env.PROFILE_SET_GH || "gh" })
    if (problems.length > 0) refuse(problems.map((message) => ({ path: "", message: `${message} — nothing moved` })))
    let state
    try {
        state = runMove(plan, { failAt: process.env.PROFILE_SET_MOVE_FAIL_AT || "" })
    } catch (e) {
        refuse([{ path: "", message: e.message }])
    }
    const result = structuredClone(profile)
    result.mode = moveTo
    if (!isObject(result.workflow)) result.workflow = {}
    result.workflow.folder = moveTo === "silent" ? plan.workflow : null
    const broken = profileProblems(result)
    if (broken.length > 0) {
        const left = undoMove(state)
        refuse(broken.map((b) => ({ ...b, message: `${b.message}; the move was rolled back${left.length ? `, except: ${left.join("; ")}` : ""}` })))
    }
    profile.mode = result.mode
    profile.workflow = result.workflow
    const report = {
        mode: moveTo,
        folder: result.workflow.folder,
        paths: plan.moves.map((m) => m.rel),
        files: plan.moves.reduce((n, m) => n + m.files.length, 0),
    }
    return { report, undo: () => undoMove(state) }
}

// --- compare-and-write, under the lock --------------------------------------------------
const { text: before, profile, fingerprint: currentFingerprint } = readProfile()
const name = nameOf(profile)
const expected = expect === "null" ? null : expect
if (expected !== currentFingerprint) {
    out(JSON.stringify({ conflict: true, fingerprint: currentFingerprint }))
    die(5, `${fields.length === 0 ? "workflow.pipeline" : WHAT} of ${pjPath} changed since it was read — not written; read it again`)
}

let moved = null
if (mode === "move") moved = moveFiles()
else if (fields.length > 0 && mode === "set") {
    // Checked again against the file under the lock: it may have changed since a --check.
    const problems = fileProblems(profile, value)
    if (problems.length > 0) refuse(problems)
    const broken = resultProblems(profile, value)
    if (broken.length > 0) refuse(broken)
    for (const f of fields) apply(profile, f, value[f])
} else if (fields.length > 0) {
    // --reset: each field removed, required or not.
    for (const f of fields) {
        const { holder, last } = holderOf(profile, f)
        if (holder !== undefined) delete holder[last]
    }
    // A removed workflow.ci_batch_run under workflow.ci "batch" is a profile bin/profile refuses.
    const broken = profileProblems(profile)
    if (broken.length > 0) refuse(broken)
} else if (mode === "set") {
    if (profile.workflow === null || typeof profile.workflow !== "object" || Array.isArray(profile.workflow)) profile.workflow = {}
    profile.workflow.pipeline = value
} else if (profile.workflow !== null && typeof profile.workflow === "object" && !Array.isArray(profile.workflow)) {
    delete profile.workflow.pipeline
}
const after = JSON.stringify(profile, null, 2) + "\n"
const fingerprint = fields.length > 0 ? fieldsFingerprint(fieldValues(profile)) : pipelineFingerprint(mode === "set" ? value : undefined)
if (after === before) {
    out(JSON.stringify({ written: false, fingerprint, warning: null }))
    process.exit(0)
}
try {
    if (moved !== null && process.env.PROFILE_SET_MOVE_FAIL_AT === "profile") throw new Error("failed at profile (PROFILE_SET_MOVE_FAIL_AT)")
    const tmp = `${pjPath}.tmp-${process.pid}`
    fs.writeFileSync(tmp, after)
    fs.renameSync(tmp, pjPath)
} catch (e) {
    if (moved === null) die(1, `cannot write ${pjPath}: ${e.message} — not written`)
    // The files moved, the profile did not: the files go back, so the profile and the files agree again.
    const left = moved.undo()
    refuse([{ path: "", message: `cannot write ${pjPath}: ${e.message}; the move was rolled back${left.length ? `, except: ${left.join("; ")}` : ""}` }])
}

// --- the commit: history, not a condition ---------------------------------------------
const run = (args) => spawnSync(GIT, args, { encoding: "utf8", windowsHide: true })
const said = (r) => (r.error ? r.error.message : (r.stderr || r.stdout || `exit ${r.status}`).trim())
const realDir = (p) => {
    try {
        return fs.realpathSync.native(p)
    } catch {
        return path.resolve(p)
    }
}
function commit() {
    const home = realDir(harnessHome(realDir(target)))
    const rel = path.relative(home, realDir(pjPath))
    if (rel.startsWith("..") || path.isAbsolute(rel)) return `${pjPath} is outside the Harness home ${home}: the change is not committed`
    const top = run(["-C", home, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"])
    if (top.error) return `git could not be started (${top.error.message}): the change is not committed`
    // A Harness home inside another repository is not a repository of its own: nothing is committed there.
    if (top.status !== 0 || realDir(top.stdout.trim()) !== home) return `no git repository in the Harness home ${home}: the change is not committed`
    const file = rel.split(path.sep).join("/")
    const add = run(["-C", home, "add", "--", file])
    if (add.status !== 0 || add.error) return `git add ${file} failed: ${said(add)}`
    // Without the machine's hooks and signing, and with an identity when it has none (as bin/project-connect).
    const args = ["-C", home, "-c", "core.hooksPath=/dev/null", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false"]
    const email = run(["-C", home, "config", "user.email"])
    if (email.status !== 0 || email.stdout.trim() === "") args.push("-c", "user.name=Harness", "-c", "user.email=harness@localhost")
    const message =
        moved !== null
            ? `Move ${name} to ${moveTo === "silent" ? "Silent" : "Full"} mode`
            : fields.length > 0
            ? `${mode === "set" ? "Set" : "Reset"} ${WHAT} of ${name}`
            : mode === "set"
              ? `Set the Pipeline of ${name}`
              : `Reset the Pipeline of ${name} to the default`
    // `-- <file>`: the commit holds profile.json only, whatever else is staged in the Harness home.
    const done = run([...args, "commit", "-q", "--no-verify", "-m", message, "--", file])
    if (done.status === 0 && !done.error) return null
    // What the failed commit staged does not stay in the index.
    run(["-C", home, "reset", "-q", "--", file])
    return `git commit failed: ${said(done)}`
}
const problem = commit()
const warning = problem === null ? null : `${problem}; the write stays`
if (warning !== null) err(`profile-set: warning: ${warning}`)
out(JSON.stringify(moved === null ? { written: true, fingerprint, warning } : { written: true, fingerprint, warning, moved: moved.report }))
